 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; FINDINGS about loci, discovered while shaping this corpus. These are not
 ;; corpus workarounds; they are things the next person will hit.
 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 :findings
 [{:about "cat-col"
   :where "src/loci/content.clj"
   :finding
   "`cat-col` sorts candidate string columns by DISTINCT COUNT ASCENDING and takes the first, so
among columns with 2-12 distinct values FEWER ALWAYS WINS — and a two-valued boolean flag beats a
nine-value taxonomy every time. USGS's `Is critical mineral 2025` (Yes/No) out-ranks `Commodity`
(9); MET's `Department` (10) out-ranks `era` (8). Nothing warns you: the table still offers Pivot
and Bar, it just pivots on the wrong axis and the coarse column you designed is inert. Two columns
were dropped from this corpus for that reason alone."}
  {:about "measure-col"
   :where "src/loci/content.clj"
   :finding
   "A column is treated as a summable quantity unless its NAME matches the rate pattern or all its
values fall in [1500, 2200]. So `Voter turnout of registered voters` passed through verbatim would
be SUMMED by the Bar viewer — percentages added together — and MET's `Object Begin Date` would be
summed too, because this extract spans -1900 to 2003 and so fails the year-like test. Both were
renamed (`turnout_pct`, `year`) to get an honest default chart."}
  {:about "line"
   :where "src/loci/content.clj"
   :finding
   "`line` looks for a series column only among #{:tenure-band :dept :channel :region :stage}. The
monthly table's coarse column is `country`, which is not in that set, so Over time draws ten
economies as one interleaved line. Left alone deliberately — Task 6 should see it."}
  {:about "col-kw and safe-event"
   :where "src/loci/substrate.clj"
   :finding
   "No header in this corpus broke anything. `col-kw` was run over every committed header and over
the source headers that were dropped — `Is critical mineral 2025`, `MCS chapter`, `LAST UPDATE`,
`Which countries have banned the use of leaded petrol in road vehicles?`, and `Key Proponent(s)`,
the header that truncated the log in July — and every one round-trips through pr-str/read-string.
`safe-event` is a no-op on all five tables. The fix holds against real data."}]

